WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.355
A new café sells cold brew.

2
00:00:05.355 --> 00:00:09.445
In its first four weeks it sells two, three

3
00:00:09.445 --> 00:00:11.900
five and six hundred cups.

4
00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.200
The owner wants a straight

5
00:00:14.275 --> 00:00:17.500
line through them, C plus D times the week

6
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.850
to see the trend.

7
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.403
The line through the first

8
00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:23.521
two weeks is two plus t.

9
00:00:23.521 --> 00:00:27.080
Will the best line be steeper or flatter?

10
00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.520
Pause and guess.

11
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.748
One equation per week gives four

12
00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:37.064
equations for two unknowns.

13
00:00:37.147 --> 00:00:39.463
The matrix A has a column of

14
00:00:39.546 --> 00:00:41.780
ones and a column of weeks.

15
00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:45.185
The first two weeks fix C equals

16
00:00:45.281 --> 00:00:47.285
two and D equals one.

17
00:00:47.285 --> 00:00:51.200
Then week two says two plus two is five.

18
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.250
It misses.

19
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.733
And week three misses too.

20
00:00:54.733 --> 00:00:57.603
b is not in the column space of A

21
00:00:57.603 --> 00:01:00.720
no line goes through all four points.

22
00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:03.604
So the question changes

23
00:01:03.604 --> 00:01:07.510
which line makes the error smallest?

24
00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:10.758
Least squares picks the x that

25
00:01:10.847 --> 00:01:12.981
makes the squared error

26
00:01:12.981 --> 00:01:16.094
the length squared of b minus A x

27
00:01:16.094 --> 00:01:18.050
as small as possible.

28
00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.489
Lecture thirteen solved exactly this.

29
00:01:21.489 --> 00:01:24.744
The closest point is the projection p

30
00:01:24.744 --> 00:01:28.000
and x hat solves the normal equations.

31
00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:32.811
For the café, A transpose A is four, six

32
00:01:32.811 --> 00:01:37.708
six, fourteen: counts and sums of the weeks.

33
00:01:37.708 --> 00:01:41.843
A transpose b is sixteen, thirty one

34
00:01:41.843 --> 00:01:43.910
sums of the sales.

35
00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:46.792
Solve: C is one point nine

36
00:01:46.792 --> 00:01:49.136
and D is one point four

37
00:01:49.136 --> 00:01:52.980
a hundred and forty more cups each week.

38
00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:55.943
Watch the line tilt from two

39
00:01:56.037 --> 00:01:58.277
plus t to the best line.

40
00:01:58.277 --> 00:02:01.730
Steeper: the later weeks pull it up.

41
00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:05.467
At the four weeks the line gives p

42
00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:08.623
one point nine, three point three

43
00:02:08.623 --> 00:02:11.870
four point seven and six point one.

44
00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:14.399
The residuals are b minus p

45
00:02:14.399 --> 00:02:17.511
the gaps between the dots and the line

46
00:02:17.511 --> 00:02:20.857
point one, minus point three, point three

47
00:02:20.857 --> 00:02:22.180
minus point one.

48
00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:25.184
Their squares add to point two

49
00:02:25.184 --> 00:02:27.067
and they add to zero

50
00:02:27.152 --> 00:02:29.121
that is e perpendicular

51
00:02:29.207 --> 00:02:31.090
to the column of ones.

52
00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.022
Continue the line to week four

53
00:02:34.022 --> 00:02:35.522
seven point five

54
00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:38.521
about seven hundred and fifty cups.

55
00:02:38.521 --> 00:02:40.520
A trend, not a promise.

56
00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:44.526
So there are two pictures of one answer.

57
00:02:44.526 --> 00:02:46.325
In the data picture

58
00:02:46.325 --> 00:02:49.580
the four residuals are vertical gaps.

59
00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.436
In Lecture thirteen's picture

60
00:02:52.436 --> 00:02:54.107
in four dimensions

61
00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:57.698
they are the four entries of one vector e

62
00:02:57.698 --> 00:03:01.290
perpendicular to the plane of the columns.

63
00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:04.439
A common slip is to measure each error

64
00:03:04.506 --> 00:03:07.008
as the shortest distance to the line

65
00:03:07.008 --> 00:03:08.630
at a right angle to it.

66
00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.522
That is not least squares.

67
00:03:11.611 --> 00:03:13.923
We use the line to predict

68
00:03:14.012 --> 00:03:15.791
sales from the week

69
00:03:15.791 --> 00:03:19.170
and a wrong prediction is wrong in y.

70
00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:22.168
So the error is the vertical gap.

71
00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:24.575
The perpendicular fit exists

72
00:03:24.655 --> 00:03:27.302
and here it gives one point eight

73
00:03:27.383 --> 00:03:29.950
seven plus one point four two t

74
00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:33.480
a different line, for a different question.

75
00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.646
A third route, by calculus.

76
00:03:36.742 --> 00:03:39.903
The squared error E is a function

77
00:03:39.998 --> 00:03:42.297
of two numbers, C and D

78
00:03:42.297 --> 00:03:44.500
a sum of four squares.

79
00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:47.595
At the minimum both partial

80
00:03:47.696 --> 00:03:49.831
derivatives are zero.

81
00:03:49.933 --> 00:03:52.982
The derivative in C gives four

82
00:03:53.084 --> 00:03:55.930
C plus six D equals sixteen.

83
00:03:56.280 --> 00:04:00.037
The derivative in D gives six C plus

84
00:04:00.142 --> 00:04:03.168
fourteen D equals thirty one.

85
00:04:03.168 --> 00:04:07.760
Those are the normal equations, row by row.

86
00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:10.169
Nudge C up by a tenth

87
00:04:10.169 --> 00:04:13.632
and the error rises above point two.

88
00:04:13.632 --> 00:04:17.094
Back to the best line: three routes

89
00:04:17.094 --> 00:04:18.030
one line.

90
00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:23.072
So when A x equals b has no solution

91
00:04:23.072 --> 00:04:26.930
solve A x hat equals p instead.

92
00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:30.559
The normal equations give the best line

93
00:04:30.559 --> 00:04:33.920
and the residuals are the vertical gaps.

94
00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.658
In part two: more columns

95
00:04:36.658 --> 00:04:40.062
one wild week that pulls the whole line

96
00:04:40.145 --> 00:04:43.133
and why training a linear regression

97
00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:45.540
is exactly this computation.
